  "summary": "Postinstall dependency-manager fetches and executes remote shell script from third-party GitHub repository",
  "details": "scripts/dependency-manager.js runs at install time and executes `execSync('curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rtk-ai/rtk/refs/heads/master/install.sh...')`, piping and running an unpinned remote shell script from a mutable master branch of a repository (`rtk-ai/rtk`) whose namespace does not match the package publisher (`@leejungkiin`). The script also reaches out to `https://www.rtk-ai.app` and `https://api.github.com`, reads `os.homedir()` and branches on `process.platform`, and uses `https.get` + `child_process` primitives during dependency resolution. Because the fetched shell script is unpinned, unverified (no hash/signature), and served from a mutable branch on a third-party namespace, whatever bytes that URL returns at install time run with the installer's privileges. Additional network/child_process primitives are present in bin/awk.js and scripts/model-manager.js.",
